    "created_at": "2025-10-29T13:36:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-29T13:36:55Z",
    "body": "Yeah this is very much intentional. If you want to share a URL object in some way, you need to share the serialized URL. This follows https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#url-apis-elsewhere.\n\nAn API for getting alternative JSON representations could be a thing I suppose, but I'd want TC39 to set precedent for how to go about that first. And some precedent in widely adopted libraries that show there's a real demand for this.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
